TRADE-OFF (any n): if the dust is to cluster at k >= 20 /Mpc physical while the background passes from 27 to 216 x today's mean (z 2 to 5),
  that stretch of n spans a clock offset of at most 1.00e-08; every well deeper than (offset of the z = 2 background) + 1.0e-08 then holds at least 216 x the mean.
  To keep wells of depth 4e-06 (the deepest spirals) below it, n must be flat between today's mean and the z = 2 density: slope <= 0.138 Mpc^-2,
  i.e. a Jeans length of at least 16.9 Mpc (physical) for z < 2. The quadratic at the CMB line has slope 3.93e+04: it floods every well.

kappa = 1/2 FITTED; not theory closed. Adopts nothing.
